            <ArticleTitle>Predictors of outcome in the treatment of chronic &quot;psychogenic&quot; pain with amitriptyline and brief psychotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Baseline measures associated with outcome are described for amitriptyline and brief psychotherapy used in the outpatient treatment of chronic &quot;psychogenic&quot; pain. The results delineate patient profiles associated with suitability for these treatments. These may serve as guidelines for choice in the treatment of heterogeneous pain clinic patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
